/*!
\page page_stmtdhit StMtdHit

\brief Reconstructed hit in the STAR Muon Telescope Detector (MTD).

\section mtdhit_overview Overview

StMtdHit represents a fully reconstructed hit in the STAR Muon Telescope Detector (MTD),
which became fully operational in Run 12 (2012) and covers |η| < 0.5.

The MTD is a scintillator-based detector mounted \b outside the STAR magnet return yoke,
purpose-built for muon identification and di-muon physics (J/ψ → μμ, ϒ → μμ).

Geometry: 30 backlegs × 5 modules × 12 cells.

Each module is read from two ends (west/east or top/bottom), providing a \c pair of
leading and trailing edge times. The time of flight is estimated as the average of the
two leading-edge times; the difference encodes the hit position along the module.

Hits are stored in \ref StMtdCollection via StEvent::mtdCollection().

\section mtdhit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code{.txt}
TObject → StObject → StMtdHit
\endcode

\section mtdhit_members Data Members

| Member | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| mBackLeg | UChar_t | Backleg number (1–30) |
| mModule | UChar_t | Module number within backleg (1–5) |
| mCell | UChar_t | Cell number within module (1–12) |
| mLeadingEdgeTime | pair<Double_t,Double_t> | Leading-edge times for both ends [ns] |
| mTrailingEdgeTime | pair<Double_t,Double_t> | Trailing-edge times for both ends [ns] |
| mAssociatedTrack | StLink<StTrack> | Matched reconstructed track |
| mIdTruth | Int_t | MC truth track ID |
| mQuality | UShort_t | MC truth quality (% charge from truth) |

tot() returns a pair: (trailing.first−leading.first, trailing.second−leading.second) [ns].
tof() returns 0.5*(leading.first + leading.second) [ns].

\section mtdhit_methods Key Methods

- backleg() — backleg number (1–30)
- module() — module number (1–5)
- cell() — cell number (1–12)
- leadingEdgeTime() — leading-edge times for both ends [ns]
- trailingEdgeTime() — trailing-edge times for both ends [ns]
- tot() — time-over-threshold pair [ns]
- tof() — estimated time of flight [ns] (average of two ends)
- associatedTrack() — pointer to matched StTrack
- idTruth(), qaTruth() — MC truth information
- setLeadingEdgeTime(pair<double,double>) — set leading-edge times

\section mtdhit_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StMtdCollection* coll = event->mtdCollection();
if (coll) {
    const StSPtrVecMtdHit& hits = coll->mtdHits();
    for (const auto& h : hits) {
        int    backleg = h->backleg();
        int    module  = h->module();
        double tof     = h->tof();       // average of two ends [ns]
        auto   leTime  = h->leadingEdgeTime();  // pair [ns]
        auto   tot     = h->tot();       // pair [ns]
        if (h->associatedTrack()) { /* muon PID */ }
    }
}
\endcode

\see StMtdRawHit, StMtdHeader, StMtdCollection
*/
